<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02E0">Remark <span data-tag="02E0">6.1.6.2</span> <span class="named">(Duals as Adjoints)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a monoidal category containing objects $X$ and $Y$, which we regard as $1$-morphisms of the bicategory $B\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ described in Example <a data-tag="00F1" href="/tag/00F1">2.2.2.5</a>. Suppose we are given a pair of morphisms </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{coev}: {\bf 1} \rightarrow Y \otimes X \quad \quad \operatorname{ev}: X \otimes Y \rightarrow {\bf 1} \]
</div>
<p> in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, which we identify with $2$-morphisms of $B\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then the pair $(\operatorname{coev}, \operatorname{ev})$ is a duality datum in the monoidal category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02DZ" href="/tag/02DZ">6.1.6.1</a>) if and only if it is an adjunction in the bicategory $B\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02CG" href="/tag/02CG">6.1.1.1</a>). </p>
</article>
